id: pm-9nfpwd
title: "GH-763: merge-decision receipt persists shell-quoted item_path that cannot resolve"
description: "The Git merge driver double-quotes %P even though Git already shell-quotes that placeholder, so conflict receipts store literal quote characters around item_path. The merge decision remains durable but its repair target cannot be opened programmatically; older clone-local driver config also survives package upgrades."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T05:33:58.913Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T08:44:23.129Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T08:17:53.884Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Generated merge-driver configuration passes %P exactly once without preserving Git shell quotes; the runtime defensively normalizes one legacy shell-quote pair; merge report and validate diagnose stale clone-local driver configuration; Linux, macOS, Windows, packed-consumer, and two-branch merge tests prove receipt paths resolve; existing receipt data remains readable."
parent: pm-o2kc
reporter: github-issue-763
severity: high
resolution: "Git merge drivers now pass the percent-P placeholder unquoted, receipt parsing removes one legacy matching quote pair, and merge installation refreshes every runtime item-type fence."
expected_result: "Every merge-decision receipt stores a repository-relative item_path that resolves directly, including in clones whose merge driver was installed by an older pm version."
actual_result: "Receipts store values such as '.agents/pm/tasks/pm-id.toon' with the single quote characters included, so the recorded path does not exist."
component: "merge:decision-receipt"
